A||||7||Uaana||Pully replacement||||5||
Z||000000||Uaana||02-04-2000||02:36 PM||||Got a question for those of you in the know.<BR>I know I have a loose belt and was thinking<BR>of replacing my pully at the same time..<BR>"saw the add from the fiero store" <BR>Do these things really give a 6% increase in<BR>hp? and how hard is it?<P>Thanks in advance.||||reg||5
Z||000001||Tim||02-04-2000||09:20 PM||||I got pulleys from ASP Racing on the net. <A HREF="http://www.autospecialties.com/gm.htm" TARGET=_blank>http://www.autospecialties.com/gm.htm</A> <BR>$79.95 plus $5 s/h for both pulleys.<BR>You can feel difference in the seat of the pants.  Do it!||||reg||1
Z||000002||Shaun41178||02-05-2000||12:23 PM||||Sorry Tim but I call BS about you statement of feeling it in the seat of the pants by using that meter.  Uaana, you will not feel a difference.  About 2 weeks ago I dyno tested the pulley and posted the results here.  Not too many people really seemed interested as there were no responses to it.  The results were +4 hp at 40 mph at full throttle.  Sorry but it wasn't graphed through the rpm range.  up to 90 though the aftermarket pulley added maybe perhaps 1 hp and sometimes was the same as the stock pulley.  I don't care who you are but you will not feel 4 hp gain.  It will be noticed in the qtr mile though as I have taken off .2 with it in the qtr mile.  I say get it.  Its a good mod and gives more power but nothing you will feel.  Now nitrous, that is something you can feel.||||reg||1
Z||000003||theogre||02-05-2000||01:16 PM||||if one of your reasons for replacing pulleys is wear, then you likely have to replace all of them. the alternator waterpump and AC compressor if present will all be worn. Leaving one worn pully on a belt is just as bad as 10 as far as belt wear goes.||||reg||1
Z||000004||Tim||02-05-2000||06:00 PM||||Shaun41178 and others:<BR>I was surprised at the improvement also.  The engine "revs" faster because the pulleys are lighter, so gives the feel.  <BR>Stock pulleys: crank=1124.9 grams  alt=156.5 grams<P>ASP pulleys: crank=316.7 grams   alt=119.7 grams<P>the stock ratio=1:2.6<BR>the ASP ratio=1:1.6<P>less weight to rotate, the engine is responsive<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000005||Formula||02-06-2000||11:13 AM||||It took me a week to find a waterpump pulley for the V6.<P>I had to order one off of here.<P>If you have a loud/amplified stereo I wouldn't reccomend the performance pulley.||||reg||1
Z||000006||penetrator||02-08-2000||09:09 AM||||How hard is it to change the pulley, is it one mans job in 1-2 hours, or 2 mans job in a week ?<P>Magnus||||reg||1
Z||000007||Shaun41178||02-08-2000||02:43 PM||||Formula: Are you talkking about a underdrive waterpump pulley?  It seems to me you weren't but I keep second guessing myself so I had to ask to be sure.<P>Penetrator:  It is a one man job and took me about 45 minutes to so.  It is very simple to do.  I have a list of directions to follow when changing the crank pulley on my webpage.  I also list the tools needed so you can have those ready when you are going to install the pulley.<BR> <A HREF="http://members.aol.com/Shaun41178" TARGET=_blank>http://members.aol.com/Shaun41178</A> <BR>is my homepage.  Just scroll down till you see the link for Underdrive pulley and click on that.  Good luck||||reg||1
